prompt:
How can I solve for "x" using the given system of equations in MATLAB, where "x = a + 2b - c/3" and "ap + bq + cr = 28" and "a + b + c = 10"?
Here is the MATLAB code to solve for "x":
syms a b c p q r x
eq1 = ap + bq + cr == 28;
eq2 = a + b + c == 10;
eq3 = x == a + 2*b - c/3;
sol = solve([eq1, eq2, eq3], [a, b, c]);
The "sol" variable will contain the solutions for "a", "b", and "c" that can be used to calculate the value of "x".

